{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Officers of thousands.</b> At the end of the first chapter of Sanhedrin it concludes that the officers of thousands were 600, the officers of hundreds were 6,000, the officers of fifty were 12,000, and the officers of tens were 60,000. And this is difficult, for when you take from Israel 18,000 and 600 for officers of thousands and officers of hundreds and officers of fifty, then there will not remain in Israel 60,000, and you will not find 60,000 for officers of tens. And one may answer that first they would select for officers of tens 60,000, and from the most distinguished among them they would select 12,000 for officers of fifty, and also from the officers of fifty they would select from the most distinguished among them 6,000 for officers of hundreds, and from them they would select 600 for officers of thousands. And as for what we say there, 'thus the judges of Israel were found to be 70,000 and 8,000 and 600' — there it is counting judges; or alternatively, the officers of tens were from the 60,000 of Israel who were from age twenty to age sixty, but the officers of thousands and officers of hundreds and officers of fifty were from the elders who were from age sixty and upward."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:26.901252524Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}